{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 13 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". This is classic counting using automaton or recurrence. Equivalent to number of binary strings of length n with no run of 3 same bits. This is Fibonacci-like. Let's compute via DP: Let a_n be number of strings length n ending with run of 1 of length 1, b_n ending with run length 2 of 1, c_n ending with run length 1 of 0, d_n ending with run length 2 of 0. Recurrence: from a_n (ending with single 1), next bit can be 0 -> c_{n+1} = a_n; or 1 -> b_{n+1} = a_n. Similarly from b_n (ending with 11), next bit can be 0 -> c_{n+1} = b_n; cannot add 1 because would make 111. From c_n (ending with single 0), next bit 1 -> a_{n+1} = c_n; 0 -> d_{n+1} = c_n. From d_n (ending with 00), next bit 1 -> a_{n+1} = d_n; cannot add 0. Base n=1: strings length1: \"0\" -> c1=1; \"1\" -> a1=1. Others zero. Compute up to n=13.\n\nLet's iterate.\n\nn=1: a=1,b=0,c=1,d=0. total=2.\n\nn=2: compute new:\na2 = c1 + d1 =1+0=1\nb2 = a1 =1\nc2 = a1 + b1 =1+0=1\nd2 = c1 =1\nCheck: total=1+1+1+1=4. Good.\n\nn=3:\na3 = c2 + d2 =1+1=2\nb3 = a2 =1\nc3 = a2 + b2 =1+1=2\nd3 = c2 =1\ntotal=2+1+2+1=6.\n\nn=4:\na4 = c3 + d3 =2+1=3\nb4 = a3 =2\nc4 = a3 + b3 =2+1=3\nd4 = c3 =2\ntotal=3+2+3+2=10.\n\nn=5:\na5 = c4 + d4 =3+2=5\nb5 = a4 =3\nc5 = a4 + b4 =3+2=5\nd5 = c4 =3\ntotal=5+3+5+3=16.\n\nn=6:\na6 = c5 + d5 =5+3=8\nb6 = a5 =5\nc6 = a5 + b5 =5+3=8\nd6 = c5 =5\ntotal=8+5+8+5=26.\n\nn=7:\na7 = c6 + d6 =8+5=13\nb7 = a6 =8\nc7 = a6 + b6 =8+5=13\nd7 = c6 =8\ntotal=13+8+13+8=42.\n\nn=8:\na8 = c7 + d7 =13+8=21\nb8 = a7 =13\nc8 = a7 + b7 =13+8=21\nd8 = c7 =13\ntotal=21+13+21+13=68.\n\nn"}}],"created":1790949071,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_token